<title>INDIA: India M3 money supply rises to 16.2 pct on Jan 31.</title>
<headline>India M3 money supply rises to 16.2 pct on Jan 31.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's year-on-year M3 money supply growth was 16.2 percent on January 31, 1997, up from 15.7 percent on January 17, 1997, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.  </p>
<p>		   M3 MONEY SUPPLY GROWTH (yr-on-yr in pct)</p>
<p>		   Jan 31, 1997   Jan 17, 1997  Feb 2,1996</p>
<p>		   16.2	     15.7	    14.28</p>
<p>Money supply was 6,716.67 billion rupees on January 31, 1997 compared to 6,655.32 billion rupees on January 17, 1997, the RBI said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
